+The builder starts suspended and is assigned to that original Windows job. Its
+PID, image, creation timestamp and BelowNormal priority are captured from the
+original process handle before Resume. It then resumes in that job and attempts
+CIM registration under the existing lease, following AnimationFF's reviewed
+Resume-before-CIM protocol. Only the exact unavailable-identity error is retried,
+every 100 ms for less than five seconds on a monotonic clock. Budget/closure
+observations continue during registration. Synchronous scheduler calls are not
+preempted; a return at or after the deadline is refused, not accepted as timely.
+Closed-before-registration, root-exited-with-descendants and unavailable identity
+are distinct outcomes; none substitutes a PID-only identity or proves a successful
+build. Failed original factory creation without a returned owner retains the lease
+because closure is unknown. All descendants, including
 MSBuild/CL/telemetry, remain in that job. Root exit plus `Active=0` is required;
 unqualified residual children after a two-second drain cause failure and an exact
 owned-job stop. No process-name kill is used. If closure cannot be confirmed,
@@ -172,6 +187,32 @@ is checked again after all getters and disk measurement, before accepting closur
 At or beyond 2,000 ms of drain, 10,000 ms of cleanup, or the global deadline, even
 a zero-active snapshot is too late. Cleanup timing begins before `Stop` itself.
 
+## First admitted attempt and registration correction
+
+The single attempt on 2026-10-12 at 06:02:05 UTC used source `2dfbbf37` and Plan
+SHA256 `d878d3423ed1c8b1ac8452a25eb06d943fd6b28b106b1a37d09f266b8f59bc55`.
+It failed with `Child identity unavailable; reservation retained.` while Python
+was still suspended. The original process handle provided identity, but the CIM
+error did not identify which inventory field was absent. Python never resumed;
+zlib initialization, configure, compilation and native tests did not run.
+Original owned stop completed with exit 122 and zero active members; the lease
+was released. The immutable ignored `build/native-reviewed-20261012/supervision.json`
+has SHA256 `9b134d6628256d72ed17f6afd8e20dcd1f97f673848e019525fe1ee5648a77bc`.
+Do not reuse this failed run root or overwrite its receipt.
+
+The local orchestration correction follows project commit
+`54a897bbf08e92ddc9ab064eb59f47c7538f89fe` and the current rig's same call ordering.
+Read-only reference SHA256 pins are:
+
+- `AnimationFF.Core.ps1`: `2cc1cf0536af0885fceec8de536c2d44402371c0bd889ed3110865225bd7db97`
+- `Build-AnimationFF.ps1`: `52f582ce66a6df645eae4062432ad342da9698eeaaad0ae178ad2bd931c09485`
+- `rig/Build-RigChain.ps1`: `9c4ae55334f0c2401759c160e7affe20bdbbd921aea2621fbb8e076b8a5e73fa`
+- `BeaconFF.Core.ps1` (original-handle identity): `b80047875a39731ea54838459fb71e0dca580c5e42284bd2749dc4b39c3a08a8`
+
+Shared providers, original BuildJob source, decoder and SDK binder are unchanged.
+A new committed source pin, fresh Plan and separate run root require coordinator
+review and another explicit GO. The previous GO authorized only the failed attempt.
